## Dataset Source

Raw FDA files were too large to upload to GitHub, so only the notebook and outputs are included in this repository.

Data source: [FDA MAUDE Database Search Portal](https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfMAUDE/search.CFM)

Files analyzed:
- MDR Event Files  
- Device Files  
- Patient Files  
- Narrative Text Files  

Time period analyzed: **2020–2025**

The MAUDE database contains adverse event reports submitted by manufacturers, importers, hospitals, healthcare professionals, and consumers for device-related injuries, malfunctions, and deaths. FDA notes that MAUDE should be used for signal detection and trend analysis—not direct failure rate comparisons. :contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0}
